  "question": {
    "text": "Which of the following would give a linear plot?\n(\\(k\\) is the rate constant of an elementary reaction and \\(\\mathrm{T}\\) is temp. in absolute scale)",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Cwfla",
      "text": "k vs T",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SCwHK",
      "text": "\\(\\mathrm{k~vs~} 1 / \\mathrm{T}\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "aPcqz",
      "text": "In k vs T",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AZh3U",
      "text": "\\(\\ln \\mathrm{k~vs~} 1 / \\mathrm{T}\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hint : Arrhenius equation gives us\n\\(\\begin{aligned}\n& k=A e^{-E_a / R T} \\\\\n& \\ln k=\\ln A-\\frac{E_a}{R}\\left(\\frac{1}{T}\\right) \\\\\n& y=c-m x\n\\end{aligned}\\)\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/uaDHSG4eZLgawC5sO8i_71PIbxQlDhol3AJMYWYr8tw.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
